## Context

Found by the round-1 reviewer of PR #1538 (ticket 1291), which resolved
audit finding 7 the same way: `docs/ncc-pipeline-audit.md:282` (finding 6,
"Nice-to-have" list) still records a defect in `structural-breaks.md`
lines 60-63 — but ticket 0290 (commit 94737720) deleted
`deliverables/_shared/_includes/structural-breaks.md` the same day it
deleted `core-vs-full.md`. An audit finding against a file that no longer
exists reads as an open defect forever; recording a defect in prose is
not a mechanism for removing it.

Finding 7 was handled one-off in 1291. The class deserves the sweep once:
the audit predates the 0290 include deletions and may carry more findings
whose subject files are gone.

## Relevant files

- `docs/ncc-pipeline-audit.md:282` — finding 6 against the deleted include.
- `git show --name-status 94737720` — the 14 deleted includes (the sweep list).

## Actions

1. Extract every file path the audit references, check each against the
   tree (and against 94737720's deletion list), and mark each orphaned
   finding resolved the way 1291 resolved finding 7: state the disposition
   (fixed earlier, or mooted by the 0290 deletion), keep the history
   git-verifiable, do not falsify the original finding.
2. Findings whose subject still exists stay untouched — this ticket only
   retires findings against files that are gone.

## Test

Prose: every file path referenced by `docs/ncc-pipeline-audit.md` either
exists in the tree or its finding is marked resolved with the deletion
recorded. `make check-fast` and `make lint` stay green.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No finding in `docs/ncc-pipeline-audit.md` reads as open against a
      file that no longer exists
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` green
